---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const description =
  'How Keep These protects private poem-making: no accounts, cookies, or poem uploads, and only aggregate visit counts.';
---

<SiteLayout
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  description={description}
  title="Privacy — Keep These"
>
  <article class="page-introduction practice-guide">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      Your unfinished work is saved only in this browser. Keep These has no
      accounts, advertising trackers, or poem uploads.
    </p>
    <p>
      To see roughly how many people visit, Keep These uses Cloudflare Web
      Analytics. It reports aggregate figures such as page views, approximate
      country, referring site, browser, device type, and page-loading
      performance. It sets no cookies, uses no persistent identifiers, does not
      follow you between sites, and never sees your poems, selections, or
      choices in the studio. Read more in
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">Cloudflare’s Web Analytics information</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      PNGs are made on your device. If you copy a poem link, its compact poem
      data sits after the <code>#</code> in the address. That fragment is used by
      your browser and is not sent to the Keep These server when the page is requested.
    </p>
    <p>
      Following a source-edition link takes you to the named external archive or
      catalogue, whose own privacy practices then apply. You can remove
      unfinished work at any time with the discard control in the studio.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
